WHY RWKV-v5/ HOLDS THE RWKV-6 KERNEL.  The archive's RWKV-v6/ directory contains a
README and nothing else; its one line reads

    "Please use /RWKV-v5/ and add --my_testing \"x060\" as an extra train.py
     parameter, to enable RWKV v6.0"

so RWKV-v5/cuda/wkv6_*.{cu,cpp} and RWKV-v5/src/model.py's RWKV_Tmix_x060 ARE
upstream RWKV-6.  This is upstream's own layout, not a guess.

HOW IT IS BUILT HERE.  Upstream compiles this pair at import time with
torch.utils.cpp_extension.load and -D_N_=<head size> -D_T_=<context length>.  That
is what kernel/cuda/rwkv_v6/upstream.py does, with the same flags upstream passes,
against these files.  See that file's header for why the repository's usual
nvcc -cubin path cannot be used for someone else's kernel.
